Q: Is there a way to make elasticsearch(5.5) autocomplete search by keyword and attribute?
A: <p>In your query you can add multiple suggesters, so for each individual field you can request suggestions. </p>

<p>If your mapping looks a bit like this:</p>

<pre><code>{
  "mappings": {
    "properties": {
      "first_name": {
        "type": "text",
        "fields": {
          "suggest": {
            "type": "completion"
          }
        }
      },
      "city": {
        "type": "text",
        "fields": {
          "suggest": {
            "type": "completion"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
</code></pre>

<p>Your query could look like this:</p>

<pre><code>POST myindex/_search
{
    "suggest": {
        "first_name_suggest" : {
            "prefix" : "phil", 
            "completion" : { 
                "field" : "first_name.suggest" 
            }
        },
        "city_suggest" : {
            "prefix" : "phil", 
            "completion" : { 
                "field" : "city.suggest" 
            }
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>

<p>See the documentation for more information about <a href="https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/5.5/search-suggesters-completion.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">completion suggesters</a> or <a href="https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/5.5/search-suggesters.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">suggesters in general</a>.</p>

